1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
A soldier is chasing emus in a truck with a machine gun on the back.

2
00:00:04,276 --> 00:00:07,125
The emus are winning. Western Australia,

3
00:00:07,346 --> 00:00:08,447
nineteen thirty-two.

4
00:00:08,899 --> 00:00:11,937
Twenty thousand emus are wrecking the wheat farms,

5
00:00:12,151 --> 00:00:14,479
so the farmers, many of them ex-soldiers,

6
00:00:14,706 --> 00:00:16,075
ask for machine guns.

7
00:00:16,379 --> 00:00:18,380
The army sends a major, two guns,

8
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:21,105
and ten thousand bullets. The plan:

9
00:00:21,404 --> 00:00:23,264
herd the emus toward the guns.

10
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,223
They scatter instead. One gun jams.

11
00:00:26,457 --> 00:00:28,443
And the truck? Too bumpy to aim.

12
00:00:28,783 --> 00:00:31,097
The army pulls out, gets sent back in,

13
00:00:31,274 --> 00:00:32,719
and shoots for weeks.

14
00:00:32,984 --> 00:00:34,065
The major's own tally?

15
00:00:34,349 --> 00:00:36,053
About ten bullets per emu.

16
00:00:36,501 --> 00:00:38,416
When farmers asked for the army again,

17
00:00:38,638 --> 00:00:41,663
the answer was no. The emus had won.
